        "glunni_faq": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Frequently Asked Questions about Glunni ACV",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "content": "<p><strong>How does Glunni ACV help people taking Ozempic, Wegovy, or Mounjaro?</strong></p><p>GLP-1 medications often slow digestion, which can cause nausea, bloating, constipation, and heartburn. Glunni ACV combines apple cider vinegar, prebiotic fiber, probiotics, and digestive enzymes to help support your digestion during this adjustment period.</p><p><strong>Can I take Glunni ACV alongside my GLP-1 medication?</strong></p><p>Many people using GLP-1 medications add Glunni ACV to their daily routine as digestive support. Since everyone responds differently, talk to your doctor before starting, especially if you're already taking other supplements or medications.</p><p><strong>How long does it take to feel a difference?</strong></p><p>Everybody responds at its own pace, but many people report feeling lighter and more comfortable digestively within the first few weeks of consistent use.</p><p><strong>Does Glunni ACV taste like vinegar?</strong></p><p>No. Unlike liquid apple cider vinegar, Glunni ACV comes in easy-to-swallow capsules — no sour taste or throat discomfort, just the benefits without the harsh flavor.</p><p><strong>Does Glunni ACV replace my GLP-1 medication?</strong></p><p>No. Glunni ACV is a dietary supplement designed to support your digestion during treatment — it does not replace, alter the dosage of, or interfere with your medication's effect.</p><p><strong>How should I take Glunni ACV?</strong></p><p>Follow the dosage on the label, taking the capsules with water, ideally close to meals. If you have any questions, consult your doctor or nutritionist.</p>"
          }
        }
